One file per car, keyed by the same id as data/vehicles.js, holding that
car's equipment list exactly as its listing on autohaus.bg prints it.

  window.AH_EQ = {
    id: "<slug>"   which car this is — vehicle.js checks it, because a stale
                   file arriving late must never be rendered against another
                   car's page.
    e:  [ ... ]    the equipment, line for line, in the listing's own order.
                   A line beginning "-" is a sub-point of the line above it.
                   A line "<code> – <text>" carries the maker's option code.
  }

SEPARATE FILES, NOT ONE TABLE. Together these are 350KB of text and a reader
wants one car's 4KB of it. vehicle.js injects exactly the one it needs, after
the page has rendered, into a section that is below the fold at every width —
so the weight is paid by the person looking at the car and by nobody else.

The per-car NOTES ("Пълна сервизна история!", "Цена без начислен 20% ДДС!",
"Възможен лизинг!" …) are NOT here. They are two to four short lines, the
price line needs them at first paint, and they live on the record itself in
data/vehicles.js. They are not the same on every car and must never be
rendered as though they were: of the 83 listings still published, 25 carry
the VAT note and 60 the service-history note.

Four of the 87 cars have no file here — their listings now return 404, i.e.
they have been sold since data/vehicles.js was scraped:
maybach-s-680-4matic, s8-plus-4-0-v8-tfsi-quattro, x7-xdrive40i-m-sport-2,
x6-m50d-xdrive-3. A car with no file renders without an equipment section;
nothing is invented to fill the gap.
